course: dictionary
lesson: 7722
title: Pudding: more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can mean different things in different places. The clues around «pudding» tell you which meaning is right. «What's for pudding?» asked after dinner means the sweet dish eaten at the end of the meal.
explain: A pudding can be soft and sweet, like rice pudding or chocolate pudding. But some puddings are not sweet at all, like Yorkshire pudding. Look at the words near the pudding to find out which kind the writer means.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Eat your peas and you'll get pudding» still makes sense if pudding means dessert, the sweet dish after the main meal.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, pudding can mean any sweet dish eaten after the main meal. People there may call it «pud».
fact: In the USA, pudding usually means a soft, creamy dessert, like chocolate pudding.
fact: A pudding is a soft, cooked dish, such as rice pudding or bread-and-butter pudding.
fact: Some puddings are not sweet: Yorkshire pudding and black pudding are examples.
fact: A Christmas pudding may have a coin hidden inside it in some stories.
exercise: «Eat your peas and you'll get pudding.» In the UK, what does pudding mean here? | A pea that has gone soft | A pot of gravy | A bowl for soup | *The sweet dish eaten after the main meal
exercise: Which of these puddings is NOT sweet? | Bread-and-butter pudding | Chocolate pudding | Rice pudding | *Yorkshire pudding
exercise: «Ollie lost his pudding.» Which word tells you the pudding is probably a dessert? | *Lost | Gravy | Ollie | Grandma
test: In the USA, what does pudding usually mean? | *A soft, creamy dessert like chocolate pudding | A savoury meat pie | A hard, crunchy biscuit | A kind of bread
test: «Christmas pudding» is an example of which kind of pudding? | A pudding that is always served cold and raw | A dish with no sugar at all | *A sweet, cooked dish | A type of gravy
exam: Which sentence is true? | *Pudding can mean a sweet dish after dinner, but some puddings are savoury | Pudding means the meal before dessert | Pudding is always black and made of sausage | Pudding can only ever mean a sweet, creamy dessert
